<name>Smart Entry &amp; Start System (Smart Entry)</name>
<para id="RM000002QX8001X" category="J" type-id="802XQ" name-id="622PK-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Smart lock and unlock do not operate from back door only</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002QX8001X_02" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002BF00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If only the door lock/unlock function by smart operation from the back door does not operate, the request code for the back door may not be transmitted. Also, since the smart function from the other doors operates, the electronic key -&gt; door control receiver communication circuit is normal. The request code transmission circuit (certification ECU -&gt; electrical key antenna) is suspected as the malfunctioning area.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (smart entry) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When using TaSCAN with the ignition switch OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON←→OFF until communication between TaSCAN and the vehicle starts. (ON←→OFF interval within 1.5 seconds)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the electrical key transmitter (electronic key) or smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) is replaced, refer to the immobiliser registration procedure in the reference section.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Check that there are no other electrical key transmitters in the vehicle interior.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002QX8001X_03" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002BG00000">
